WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.958 --> 00:00:03.460
- Chootz-pah.
- Hootz-pah.

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:04.419
- Ah.
- Chutzpah.

00:00:04.419 --> 00:00:06.004
- Heh heh heh heh heh!

00:00:06.004 --> 00:00:07.923
- That was an interesting laugh
to do during a broadcast

00:00:07.923 --> 00:00:09.841
but I appreciate your energy.

00:00:09.841 --> 00:00:11.426
-Oh, you have nice hair.

00:00:12.177 --> 00:00:13.178
It's very nice hair.

00:00:13.178 --> 00:00:15.013
♪♪

00:00:17.557 --> 00:00:21.478
I am so excited for them to see
what we did with Tarik Cohen.

00:00:21.478 --> 00:00:23.105
Welcome to "Simms &amp; Lefkoe."

00:00:23.105 --> 00:00:25.232
- It's gonna be pretty awesome.
- Dude, wasn't it?

00:00:25.232 --> 00:00:26.566
- Yes, it was. It was special.

00:00:26.566 --> 00:00:27.943
- Like, Tarik Cohen—

00:00:27.943 --> 00:00:30.153
- What a good sport, for one.
- Just stick around.

00:00:30.153 --> 00:00:31.530
You're gonna love it.
- Yes.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.824
- The thing that captured
everybody's attention

00:00:33.824 --> 00:00:35.617
this weekend, though,
wasn't even the games.

00:00:35.617 --> 00:00:39.204
It was Lil Wayne
and Odell Beckham

00:00:39.204 --> 00:00:42.040
hangin' out with the players'
reporter Josina Anderson

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:45.836
and Odell takin' a truth serum
and talking about Eli Manning.

00:00:45.836 --> 00:00:47.462
Here's a little bit
of what he said.

00:00:47.462 --> 00:00:49.798
- He's not gonna get out
the park, he's not—

00:00:49.798 --> 00:00:52.050
We know Eli's not runnin'.
- [Shakes head]

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.844
- But is it a matter of time
if you can—

00:00:53.844 --> 00:00:55.095
Can he still throw it?

00:00:55.095 --> 00:00:56.669
Yeah, he's been pretty safe.

00:00:56.669 --> 00:00:58.346
- We have been saying this
for three years.
- Yes.

00:00:58.348 --> 00:01:00.559
We've been tryin'
to keep it real—
- Right.

00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:01.810
- But when Odell does it,
it kinda goes wrong.

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:02.978
- Yes.
- It's as though he was

00:01:02.978 --> 00:01:06.732
in the movie "Liar Liar,"
a favorite of us two.

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:10.652
- The pen is
rah-rah-rah-rah-royal blue!

00:01:10.652 --> 00:01:14.239
- So we wondered,
what if all NFL players

00:01:14.239 --> 00:01:15.824
had to tell the truth?

00:01:15.824 --> 00:01:18.801
♪♪

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:21.267
All right, I'm gonna go first.
Jerry Jones to Jason Garrett.

00:01:21.267 --> 00:01:23.503
Afterwards, he said, "You know,
we gotta risk it there."

00:01:23.503 --> 00:01:25.279
Jason, still standin' by him.

00:01:25.279 --> 00:01:26.909
What he really wanted to say is,

00:01:26.909 --> 00:01:28.822
[Texan accent] "Hey, hey, Jason,
lean in real close.

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.636
You know the millions
I'm spendin' on that O-line?

00:01:30.636 --> 00:01:31.981
And you're gonna punt?

00:01:31.981 --> 00:01:34.098
I'm 'bout to punt you
back to Princeton

00:01:34.098 --> 00:01:36.340
if you come with that nonsense
one more time.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:39.238
I got Dak, I got Zeke,
I'm about to call Dez

00:01:39.238 --> 00:01:41.397
and let him yell in your face
if that's gonna help ya

00:01:41.397 --> 00:01:43.347
but I got a problem
with you, JG."

00:01:43.347 --> 00:01:44.754
- [Laughing] That's pretty good.

00:01:44.754 --> 00:01:45.995
- I'm workin' on my accent.

00:01:45.995 --> 00:01:47.277
- That sounds pretty good.
I like it.

00:01:47.277 --> 00:01:48.508
I was down in Texas before.

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.654
Oh, OK.
- Oh, Ramsey to Bortles.

00:01:50.654 --> 00:01:52.271
- A little bromance.

00:01:52.271 --> 00:01:54.890
Here's Jalen Ramsey
congratulating Blake Bortles

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:56.402
but what he's really saying is,
"Hey, Blake

00:01:56.402 --> 00:01:57.830
just don't throw interceptions!

00:01:57.830 --> 00:01:59.530
Don't even care
about incompletions

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:00.927
go 'O' for the day.
Doesn't matter!

00:02:00.927 --> 00:02:03.044
You're obviously
a little off-target today

00:02:03.044 --> 00:02:05.536
cuz you missed me on
our high-five handshake there.

00:02:05.536 --> 00:02:06.818
You're a little off there.

00:02:06.818 --> 00:02:08.841
But as long as you don't
turn it over

00:02:08.841 --> 00:02:11.145
we can win the game,
even without you."

00:02:11.145 --> 00:02:12.376
- All right, next one.

00:02:12.376 --> 00:02:14.200
Matt Ryan to Dan Quinn.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.181
Matt Ryan's sayin',
"Dan, let's figure

00:02:16.181 --> 00:02:17.871
this defense out. Catch up."

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:20.801
What he really wants to say is,
"Hey, Danny boy, I put up

00:02:20.801 --> 00:02:23.585
90 points the last three games,
and it doesn't matter

00:02:23.585 --> 00:02:26.953
cuz you've allowed 121!

00:02:26.953 --> 00:02:28.444
Your defense stinks!

00:02:28.444 --> 00:02:30.039
You've lost all these players

00:02:30.039 --> 00:02:32.219
and you're still runnin'
the same scheme!

00:02:32.219 --> 00:02:33.772
You're a defensive coach!

00:02:33.772 --> 00:02:35.128
Can I get some help, please?"

00:02:35.128 --> 00:02:36.586
- "Can I get some creativity?"
- "Please!"

00:02:36.586 --> 00:02:37.889
- "Please!" All right.

00:02:37.889 --> 00:02:39.931
Now we got the greatest
of all time.

00:02:39.931 --> 00:02:40.997
- Yeah, A-Rod.

00:02:40.997 --> 00:02:42.696
- You know, he's tryin'
to console his kicker.

00:02:42.696 --> 00:02:45.635
Guy went 0-for-4 in field goals
and a missed extra point.

00:02:45.635 --> 00:02:48.089
But you know what he really
wanted to say, Lefkoe?

00:02:48.089 --> 00:02:49.403
Come over here. Don't flinch.

00:02:49.403 --> 00:02:50.675
It's OK.
- What does he wanna say?

00:02:50.675 --> 00:02:53.198
- He wants to say,
"Oh, you have nice hair.

00:02:53.198 --> 00:02:54.773
It's very nice hair."

00:02:54.773 --> 00:02:56.029
But then he wants to go,

00:02:56.029 --> 00:02:57.890
"Are you f--king kidding me,
dude?

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:59.913
I mean, what the f--k?

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.821
I carry this team
for 10 years straight.

00:03:01.821 --> 00:03:03.354
I'm out here playin' on one leg.

00:03:03.354 --> 00:03:05.596
All you gotta do
is kick the f--king ball

00:03:05.596 --> 00:03:07.212
between the two yellow sticks.

00:03:07.212 --> 00:03:09.714
If you do that again,
you're outta here.

00:03:09.714 --> 00:03:14.499
I will tell McCarthy to cut you
in three seconds."

00:03:14.499 --> 00:03:17.681
- So, if we have to be honest
right now

00:03:17.681 --> 00:03:19.433
because we talked about
Jim Carrey earlier

00:03:19.431 --> 00:03:21.123
I would like to admit
to all of you

00:03:21.123 --> 00:03:22.687
this is an honest take

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:25.752
I believe that "Ace Ventura 2:
When Nature Calls"

00:03:25.752 --> 00:03:28.192
is one of the five
greatest movies of all time.

00:03:28.192 --> 00:03:31.112
- Oh, my gosh.
That is just beyond stupid.

00:03:31.112 --> 00:03:32.760
I don't even know what to say.
- I know you guys agree with me.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:34.282
Fill the comment section below
with support.

00:03:34.282 --> 00:03:36.180
- It's not even the best
"Ace Ventura" movie.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.869
I mean, that's what's hilarious.
- Why?

00:03:37.869 --> 00:03:39.746
Because one has Dan Marino
and a dolphin?

00:03:39.746 --> 00:03:41.038
- Oh, that was it,
that's exactly right.

00:03:41.038 --> 00:03:42.269
- 2 was in a jungle—
- Oh!

00:03:42.269 --> 00:03:43.562
- There's a white bat—

00:03:43.562 --> 00:03:45.418
- Whoa!
- And we had "guano bowls."

00:03:45.418 --> 00:03:47.086
- And nothing funny
the whole movie.

00:03:47.086 --> 00:03:49.150
That is amazing.
- Like a glove!

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:51.528
- Which came from 1.
- No, it was in 2.

00:03:51.528 --> 00:03:53.530
Oh, this is a lovely
room of death.

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:55.427
- But "like a glove"
came from 1.

00:03:55.427 --> 00:03:56.637
- Listen.
- Yeah.

00:03:56.637 --> 00:03:57.846
- We all
came from somewhere.

00:03:57.846 --> 00:03:58.950
- I mean, grow up.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:01.015
- And I thought Tarik Cohen
came from a Jewish background.

00:04:01.016 --> 00:04:02.288
Boy, was I wrong.

00:04:02.288 --> 00:04:04.248
So what I wanted to do
with Tarik Cohen

00:04:04.248 --> 00:04:07.772
was to share my Jewish culture
and experience with him.

00:04:07.772 --> 00:04:10.129
It's kind of a Bear mitzvah.

00:04:10.129 --> 00:04:11.651
Enjoy.

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:13.612
Tarik Cohen's comin' to New York
to eat

00:04:13.612 --> 00:04:15.489
at a Jewish deli
with Simms and Lefkoe?

00:04:15.489 --> 00:04:16.636
Oy vey!

00:04:16.636 --> 00:04:20.848
♪♪

00:04:22.371 --> 00:04:25.249
When I heard there was a guy
in the NFL, Simms

00:04:25.249 --> 00:04:28.064
named Tarik Cohen,
I said, "Mwah.

00:04:28.064 --> 00:04:29.753
L'chaim. We've got ourselves

00:04:29.753 --> 00:04:32.569
finally, a Jewish running back,"
and then I found out

00:04:32.569 --> 00:04:35.884
not only have you never been
to a bar mitzvah

00:04:35.884 --> 00:04:38.950
not only have you never had
Jewish food, you're not Jewish.

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:40.827
- Sadly, no.
- Sadly, no.

00:04:40.827 --> 00:04:42.286
I appreciate the "sadly."
- Yeah.

00:04:42.286 --> 00:04:43.954
- "Cohen" though.

00:04:43.954 --> 00:04:45.414
I mean, that's in the
Mount Rushmore of Jewish names.

00:04:45.414 --> 00:04:47.729
- It really is.
- I am 100 percent Jewish.

00:04:47.729 --> 00:04:49.543
- Yeah.
- What I want to give to you

00:04:49.543 --> 00:04:54.704
is the full Jewish experience.
I can call it a Jewish combine

00:04:54.704 --> 00:04:57.686
to making you feel
like a true Jewish man.

00:04:57.686 --> 00:04:59.417
Are you ready to take
this journey with me?

00:04:59.417 --> 00:05:02.191
- Oh, yeah, I'm definitely ready.
- OK.

00:05:02.191 --> 00:05:03.421
- L'chaim.

00:05:03.421 --> 00:05:04.765
- L'chaim!
- L'chaim.

00:05:04.765 --> 00:05:07.382
♪♪

00:05:08.573 --> 00:05:10.440
[Bell dinging]

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:11.847
- This is our first dish.

00:05:11.847 --> 00:05:14.840
This is a customary
Jewish breakfast.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:16.206
Do you want to take a guess
as to what

00:05:16.206 --> 00:05:17.686
is in front of you right now?

00:05:17.686 --> 00:05:19.595
- Sushi.
- Sushi.

00:05:19.595 --> 00:05:22.712
It is not sushi.
It is smoked salmon.

00:05:22.712 --> 00:05:23.953
What do you think of it?

00:05:23.953 --> 00:05:25.819
- Cream cheese and fish?
- Exactly.

00:05:25.819 --> 00:05:27.477
- Man.
- Yes, "man" is right.

00:05:27.477 --> 00:05:28.947
- All right, so
don't be afraid of it.

00:05:28.947 --> 00:05:31.961
- No, I'm not.
- So why don't you pick it up?

00:05:31.961 --> 00:05:33.462
- Oh, that was a——oh, my gosh.

00:05:33.462 --> 00:05:34.756
- Hold on.

00:05:38.172 --> 00:05:39.541
- I don't like it.

00:05:39.541 --> 00:05:41.449
- You don't?
Do you mind if I have a bite?

00:05:41.449 --> 00:05:42.826
- Damn.
- You can have all the bites.

00:05:42.826 --> 00:05:46.486
- Ugh.
- I mean, it's perfect.

00:05:46.486 --> 00:05:51.689
This is a Jewish deli staple,
and it's not just what it is—

00:05:51.689 --> 00:05:54.150
- [Laughing] His eyes.
- It's the size of it, OK?

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:57.392
- Yeah.
- This is a pastrami on rye.

00:05:57.387 --> 00:06:00.365
And do you see
how much meat is on that?

00:06:00.365 --> 00:06:02.054
- Yeah.
- That's not just special.

00:06:02.054 --> 00:06:03.650
- It's a little excessive.
- Can't miss it.

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:04.692
- He looked at that like it was

00:06:04.692 --> 00:06:05.765
a blitzing linebacker
when it came in.

00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:08.535
He, like, literally looked at it
and was like—

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:09.895
- Why don't you bite into that?
- All right.

00:06:09.895 --> 00:06:11.690
Let's see, which one—hmm.

00:06:11.699 --> 00:06:12.751
- And this is part of the process,
too

00:06:12.751 --> 00:06:14.471
the strategy of how
to bite the sandwich.

00:06:14.471 --> 00:06:16.004
- I can see that.

00:06:17.322 --> 00:06:18.747
- I'm gonna go ahead
and try to flatten him.

00:06:18.747 --> 00:06:20.435
- Nice.
I think he's gonna like this.

00:06:20.437 --> 00:06:21.291
- You think he'll like it?

00:06:21.291 --> 00:06:23.027
- I feel pretty
confident about it.

00:06:23.027 --> 00:06:24.395
- I really give him credit
for havin' the guts

00:06:24.399 --> 00:06:26.099
to just dive in there, though.

00:06:26.099 --> 00:06:27.923
- Why is there no cheese
or nothin' on it though?

00:06:27.923 --> 00:06:29.790
Cheese, mayonnaise
or somethin'?

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:33.064
- Well, that wouldn't be kosher.
We have one more.

00:06:33.064 --> 00:06:36.599
This is the Cadillac
of Jewish food.

00:06:36.599 --> 00:06:39.736
Tarik Cohen,
I'd like to introduce you

00:06:39.736 --> 00:06:45.138
to your new favorite food,
matzo ball soup.

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:47.588
- Matzo ball.
- Matzo ball.

00:06:47.588 --> 00:06:49.288
Have you heard
of matzo balls before?

00:06:49.288 --> 00:06:51.467
- Mozzarella?
- Mozzarella

00:06:51.467 --> 00:06:53.667
not the same thing.
This is not cheese.

00:06:53.667 --> 00:06:55.575
- There's no cheese in there?
- There's no cheese.

00:06:55.575 --> 00:06:57.066
You thought matzo balls
had cheese, too?

00:06:57.066 --> 00:06:59.141
- I totally did.
- So the best way to do this

00:06:59.141 --> 00:07:00.569
is to take your spoon

00:07:00.569 --> 00:07:02.206
take a little piece
of the matzo ball

00:07:02.206 --> 00:07:03.927
get a little bit
of soup in there.

00:07:03.927 --> 00:07:06.336
- Oh, it's soft.
- It's very soft.

00:07:06.336 --> 00:07:08.326
♪♪

00:07:08.326 --> 00:07:09.557
And there it is.

00:07:09.557 --> 00:07:10.964
- That's good.
- That's the 10 out of 10.

00:07:10.964 --> 00:07:12.205
- It's like chicken noodle soup,
really.

00:07:12.205 --> 00:07:13.425
- It's chicken noodle soup.

00:07:13.425 --> 00:07:17.064
♪♪

00:07:17.889 --> 00:07:21.601
The second part of our
Jewish combine is Jewish slang.

00:07:21.601 --> 00:07:23.092
- OK.
- Not only do I want you to eat

00:07:23.092 --> 00:07:25.835
like a Jew,
I want you to talk like a Jew.

00:07:25.835 --> 00:07:27.972
So here's the first word.
- This is gonna be fun.

00:07:27.972 --> 00:07:29.839
- It is.
- Schmooth.

00:07:29.839 --> 00:07:31.550
- Schmooze.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:32.916
What do you
think schmooze means?

00:07:32.916 --> 00:07:34.407
- Good sleep.
- Good sleep?

00:07:34.407 --> 00:07:35.845
Oh, like a—

00:07:35.845 --> 00:07:37.493
- Man, I'mma go schmooze.
- I'mma go schmooze.

00:07:37.493 --> 00:07:39.651
- I'm about to schmooze.
- So, a schmooze is actually

00:07:39.651 --> 00:07:41.726
to, like, kinda
talk somebody up.

00:07:41.726 --> 00:07:43.332
- "Hey, I like your play calls,
Matt Nagy."
- Yeah.

00:07:43.332 --> 00:07:45.198
- "That's a really creative one."
- "Throw me the ball."

00:07:45.198 --> 00:07:46.752
- You're schmoozing him so he
gives you the ball.
- You're schmoozing, yeah.

00:07:46.752 --> 00:07:48.066
- You schmooze, you win.
- Right.

00:07:48.066 --> 00:07:50.089
- Next word. Ooh!

00:07:50.089 --> 00:07:53.322
Good luck sayin' this one.

00:07:53.322 --> 00:07:55.773
- Chootz-pah.
- Hootz-pah.

00:07:55.773 --> 00:07:57.118
- Ah, chutzpah.

00:07:57.118 --> 00:08:00.235
- You gotta get a "heh."
- Chutzpah!

00:08:00.235 --> 00:08:02.331
- Oh!
- "We were in the team meeting

00:08:02.331 --> 00:08:03.939
and Tarik Cohen stood up
and said

00:08:03.946 --> 00:08:05.474
'I don't like that play.'

00:08:05.479 --> 00:08:07.930
Tarik's got a lot of chutzpah."

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:09.225
- Like, balls.
- Yeah.

00:08:09.225 --> 00:08:16.376
- Exactly. This is the Jewish
slang phrase of all generations.

00:08:16.376 --> 00:08:18.118
- Oy vey.
- Oy vey.

00:08:18.118 --> 00:08:19.567
What do you think it is?

00:08:19.567 --> 00:08:21.976
- "Tarik Cohen was supposed to run
the slant route

00:08:21.976 --> 00:08:23.717
and he ran the go route.

00:08:23.717 --> 00:08:25.323
Oy vey, Tarik Cohen."

00:08:25.323 --> 00:08:28.107
- Or it's like,
"All those pickles for me?

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:29.337
Oy vey."
- Oh, yeah, I got you.

00:08:29.337 --> 00:08:30.995
So it's good and bad.

00:08:30.995 --> 00:08:32.507
- It can be everything.
- OK, good.

00:08:32.507 --> 00:08:33.789
That's the one
I'mma use right there.

00:08:33.789 --> 00:08:35.562
- You have aced
the Jewish combine.

00:08:35.562 --> 00:08:37.056
And I have a gift for you.

00:08:37.056 --> 00:08:38.808
- Oy vey.
- Oy vey.

00:08:38.808 --> 00:08:41.603
I give you
a Chicago Bears yarmulke.

00:08:41.603 --> 00:08:45.732
- It's a Jewish fitted cap.
- A Jewish fitted cap, yes.

00:08:45.732 --> 00:08:47.692
Oh, my gosh,
it looks so beautiful.

00:08:47.692 --> 00:08:49.360
- Perfect.
- Simms, you're not out of here.

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:50.987
- Oooh.
- A Giants yarmulke.

00:08:50.987 --> 00:08:53.364
- I like it.
- Put that bad boy on.

00:08:53.364 --> 00:08:57.243
- Yeah!
- And I have an Eagles yarmulke.
Now we celebrate.

00:08:57.243 --> 00:08:59.412
Let's give it up for him.

00:08:59.412 --> 00:09:06.044
- Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:09:06.044 --> 00:09:07.921
- Hey!
- L'chaim!

00:09:08.379 --> 00:09:10.924
- Tarik Cohen, buddy, l'chaim!

00:09:10.924 --> 00:09:13.218
